    <feedback override="true" type="org.blockml.bml.type.Text">
      <value>Execute created a 6-block library domain model in package org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.library, matching the requested task. Only playground/library/ files were added; the pending->running move of the ModelTransformation is normal pipeline lifecycle, not an errant model edit.

Structure: Library is the aggregate root owning books, members, authors and borrowings via &lt;aggregations> (so Borrowing is managed library state, not a property of Book/Member - requirement met). Book.authors and Borrowing.member/Borrowing.book are non-owning &lt;associations> typed InstanceReference(T)[] / InstanceReference(T); Author and Member are owned only by Library, so authors/members outlive books and can be shared (requirement met). AvailabilityStatus is an EnumType with Available/Borrowed members. Every important block has concise &lt;documentation>.

Convention check against the effective model (@blockml/core, @machineblocks/core): property syntax (&lt;title type="type:Text">&lt;documentation>...) matches mbt:Connector; enum values composition matches mbt:Gender/Direction; association type shape matches def:AssociationDefinition rules (InstanceReference(T) or InstanceReference(T)[], T extends core:Block - satisfied). Package has no Library.bml catalog registration, consistent with the sibling playground/Joke.bml precedent (loose playground files).

Potential issues to review:
1. baseType choice. Book/Member/Author/Borrowing/Library extend core:Block directly. core:Block is abstract and documents 'not used directly as a composition instance type'; core:Entity is the documented branch for 'Blocks that represent instances with identity in composition or aggregation. Domain blocks ... extend Entity' (and @machineblocks domain Block extends core:Entity). If validation rejects extending core:Block for instantiable domain types, switch these five to core:Entity.
2. Cardinality semantics only partially enforced. 'A book has one or more authors' and 'a borrowing connects exactly one member and one book' are expressed as 0..n / 0..1 associations plus prose; BlockML associations cannot express 1..1 / 1..n, so the mandatory-minimum is documentation-only. 'A book can only be borrowed by one member at a time' (uniqueness of the active borrowing per book) is likewise prose in Book/Borrowing docs, not a constraint. Consider whether a Constraint sub-type should back these rules.
3. Book has both a status property (AvailabilityStatus) and the implied borrowing link - these can drift out of sync; nothing keeps status=Borrowed iff an active Borrowing references the book.

Validation NOT re-run: this Reflect stage is read-only and Bash is disabled, and Execute's own stdout in the pipeline log is truncated, so I cannot confirm `npx blockml validate` passed. Recommend the next stage run `npx blockml validate` (and `--all` since node_modules types are referenced) before completing.</value>
    </feedback>
